## 5. DESIGN SYSTEM
 
### Typography
```
Body:     Inter (Google Fonts, subsets: latin, latin-ext)
Logo:     wildloops-bold_w.ttf → var(--font-logo) → font-(family-name:--font-logo)
```

### Logo Wordmark Safety (Wild-Loops)
```
For every visible "Miur" logo wordmark using Wild-Loops:
1) Always add class `brand-logo-wordmark` (defined in app/globals.css)
2) Never use negative tracking (`tracking-tight`, `tracking-tighter`, custom negative letter-spacing)
3) Keep container compatible with swashes: no clipping on x-axis for logo wrappers
4) If creating a new logo placement, reuse existing pattern from Hero/Navbar/Footer instead of custom one-off styles
```
 
### Color Palette (zinc-based neutrals)
```css
/* Defined in globals.css :root */
--background: #ffffff
--foreground: #09090b
--primary: #18181b        /* zinc-900 */
--primary-foreground: #fafafa
--secondary: #f4f4f5      /* zinc-100 */
--muted: #f4f4f5
--muted-foreground: #71717a  /* zinc-500 */
--border: #e4e4e7         /* zinc-200 */
--radius: 0.5rem
```
 
### Tailwind Zinc Scale Usage
```
zinc-900  → primary text, buttons, headings
zinc-600  → body text, descriptions
zinc-500  → labels, captions, muted text (⚠️ minimum for WCAG AA body text)
zinc-400  → decorative, borders (⚠️ NOT for text — fails WCAG contrast)
zinc-200  → borders, dividers
zinc-100  → subtle backgrounds
zinc-50   → section backgrounds
white     → page background
```
 
### Spacing Rhythm
```
Micro:    gap-2, gap-3 (4-12px) — within components
Small:    gap-4, gap-6 (16-24px) — between elements
Medium:   gap-8, gap-12 (32-48px) — between sections within a block
Large:    py-16, py-24 (64-96px) — section padding
XL:       py-32, py-40+ (128px+) — hero-level spacing
```
 
### Typography Scale (actual usage in codebase)
```
text-[8px]   tracking-[0.5em]   → micro labels, scroll indicators
text-[9px]   tracking-[0.3em]   → navigation links, legal text
text-[10px]  tracking-[0.2em]   → section labels, uppercase tags
text-xs      (12px)              → card descriptions, secondary info
text-sm      (14px)              → body text, form labels
text-base    (16px)              → primary body text
text-xl/2xl                     → card headings
text-3xl/4xl/5xl                → section headings
text-[14vw]                     → hero display text (responsive)
```
 
### Aesthetic Principles
```
1. EDITORIAL MINIMALISM — every element earns its place
2. WHITESPACE IS A FEATURE — generous padding, breathing room
3. UPPERCASE + TRACKING — section labels always uppercase + widest tracking
4. THIN BORDERS — border-zinc-200, never heavy shadows
5. HOVER = OPACITY — preferred hover state: hover:opacity-50 transition-opacity
6. ROUNDED-FULL — pills and icon buttons always fully rounded
7. SCALE ON SCROLL — use framer-motion for parallax/scale effects
8. MONOCHROME FIRST — zinc palette dominant, color used sparingly
```
 
